                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I picked this up for a dollar so I'm not complaining. I'm not even going to seek a refund. However, in it's current state, this is utterly unplayable.\n\nHere's what you can do in AGP: You can run around. You can walk around. You can get chased by enemies. You can reload your weapon. You can dry click your gun at enemies(because the gun refuses to fire, always!). You can somehow despawn your weapon while your character model acts like he's still holding said weapon. You can open crates to get cash. You can repeatedly farm those same crates because they are on an endless regen cycle. You can spend that cash on useless skills(useless - not meaning lame. useless - meaning not functional).\n\nHere's what you can't do in AGP: Anything at all. Skills don't seem to function. The weapon doesn't function. your ability to look around with the camera sometimes ceases to function.\n\nAt somepoint there could be something here. I hope that the dollar I spent helps the development. Problem is there isn't enough here to make me wish I gave more to the cause. This is highly not recommended in it's current state. This is a classic case of too early for EA.",
